# =============================================================================
# geometry/cryosuction/openface_2D_box60um_disc_offcenter.opts
#
# Open-face verification (stage 0, test A1/A2; studies/cryosuction/README.md).
# Pure curvature flow (the experiment sets -decouple_phase_change 1), so the
# ice area has an analytic law: dA/dt = -D * (total turning of the interface),
# D = eps^2/tau_sub. eps and Nx/Ny are from comp_eps.py (written with --patch,
# 2026-11-04), alpha_c 1e-2, default v_n (curvature flow is far slower):
#   comp_eps.py --Lx 6.0e-5 --Ly 4.5e-5 --Rave 1.5e-5 --T0 -20 --alpha 1e-2
#   -> B-KINETIC binding, -eps 6.3921e-07 (h = 4.52e-7 m), all checks OK
#
# A disc R0 = 15 um centered 7.5 um OUTSIDE the open x = 0 face, so the face
# cuts it off-center and the interface meets the face at about 60 deg, not 90.
# Open face (A1): the visible part shrinks as the full disc would. Neumann
# face (A2, -phi_open_bc 0): the face forces 90 deg and the area law changes.
# =============================================================================
-ic_type multi_grains
-dim 2
-Nz 1
-Lz 0
-eps 6.3921e-07
-eps_valid_temp -20.0
-delt_t 1.0e-4
-periodic 0
# dtmax = 2*tau_sub for alpha_c 1e-2 (-beta_sub0 7.9408e5): tau_sub = 3.5952e2 s,
# printed by the solver for this eps (studies/cryosuction/scripts/preflight.sh).
# A different alpha_c or eps needs a new value.
-dtmax 7.19e2
-Nx 133
-Ny 100
-Lx 6.0e-5
-Ly 4.5e-5
-ice_grain_cx -7.5e-6
-ice_grain_cy 2.25e-5
-ice_grain_R  1.5e-5
